## 0. TOM'S MARKET STATE TAXONOMY

Tom defines two primary market states: **balance** and **trend** (imbalance).
These are not arbitrary labels — they describe whether supply and demand are in equilibrium.

> "where the market is in balance, everyone is satisfied. And where the market is out of balance, there is often dissatisfaction among the big players."
> **Source GPS:** YmygDgtoxO8 | [BEGINNING]

Tom further subdivides **trend** into three structure types.

**[FLAGGED]** The terms "range" and "volatile" appear in the MTS architecture as separate states, but Tom treats "range" as synonymous with balance/sideways and "volatile" as a market characteristic, not a formal state. This document uses Tom's exact taxonomy.

---

## 1. BALANCE (Sideways / Range / Equilibrium)

### 1.1 Definition

> "Sideways means that supply and demand are in balance. And when supply and demand are balanced, the market will always try to return to that equilibrium."
> **Source GPS:** BVpYGKz9PBU | [BEGINNING] — Trend Structure & Weekly Profile

> "where the market is in balance, everyone is satisfied."
> **Source GPS:** YmygDgtoxO8 | [BEGINNING] — Balance vs Imbalance

> "we have a beautiful balance profile here. And balance profile means the probability is high for now that the market will repeatedly try to play in balance."
> **Source GPS:** zQTbdEweG3c | [MIDDLE] — Zone Identification

### 1.2 Identification Criteria

**A. Visual / Structural**
- Market is moving back and forth, not making sustained directional moves.
- Volume profile shows a clear POC with volume concentrated around a price area.
- Price oscillates around the POC / VWAP without sustained breaks.

> "The market is moving back and forth. This week as well we have been moving sideways so far."
> **Source GPS:** BVpYGKz9PBU | [BEGINNING]

> "if you see that a market has spent a lot of time at a certain price range, the probability is relatively high that a lot of trades have also taken place there."
> **Source GPS:** YmygDgtoxO8 | [BEGINNING]

**B. Volume Profile Shape**
- B profile = balance (bell-shaped, volume concentrated at POC).
- P profile = one-sided move, often transitions from or into balance.

> "here is a B profile and that shows me that there is weakness in the market."
> **Source GPS:** BVpYGKz9PBU | [MIDDLE]

**C. Quick Watch Method**
- Even a simple line chart is sufficient for the first assessment.

> "The first thing I generally do is I give myself what I always call a quick watch of the current price trend. And for that, even a line chart would be enough because what kind of information does it give me? It tells me immediately, are we currently more in balance or are we more in a trend right now?"
> **Source GPS:** 3o1VVsfBmmU | [BEGINNING]

> "You can pinpoint that by counting closing prices or by all sorts of other means."
> **Source GPS:** 3o1VVsfBmmU | [BEGINNING]

**D. VWAP Context**
- VWAP is oriented sideways; price oscillates around it.

> "if you're someone who does very dynamic scalping, then the VWAP can be very sideways oriented."
> **Source GPS:** 43JaKHRvxHk | [END]

### 1.3 Timeframe Context

- **Weekly profile:** Shows if the overall macro structure is balanced. "The market is moving back and forth" across weekly candles.
- **Daily profile:** Shows current session balance. Prior day VAL/VAH/VPOC define the balance zone.
- **Intraday:** Price oscillates around daily POC/VWAP.

> "The weekly profiles show me immediately if the V POX are rising, staying the same or even falling... try drawing a trend based only on the V POX and the value areas and you'll find that you can immediately see if a market is flattening out in terms of global money flow or not."
> **Source GPS:** Ld1dhjGdTCA | [MIDDLE] — Point 4

### 1.4 Valid Setups in Balance

| Setup Type | Why Valid | Source |
|-----------|-----------|--------|
| Counter-Trade | Primary strategy in balance. Short at top of range, long at bottom. | BVpYGKz9PBU |
| Scalp | Trade oscillations around VWAP/POC. | 43JaKHRvxHk |
| Breakout | Only when balance is about to resolve (proof required). | zQTbdEweG3c |

> "I can definitely look for short trades up here and long trades down here. And I'll keep doing that until either the big player here or the big players here decide that the market will continue to go long."
> **Source GPS:** BVpYGKz9PBU | [BEGINNING]

> "if you're a scalper, for example, you can brilliantly search for short trades here in these price ranges. And you can search for long trades down"
> **Source GPS:** 43JaKHRvxHk | [MIDDLE]

### 1.5 Key Probability

> "And this is the case in about 70% of market phases. That's just something you need to know."
> **Source GPS:** YmygDgtoxO8 | [BEGINNING]

**Tier:** T3 — Tom's stated statistic. Not independently verified.

