## 6. GAPS — WHAT TOM DOES NOT ADDRESS

| Gap | Impact |
|-----|--------|
| Exact quantitative thresholds for fast vs normal vs slow trend | Classification is visual/experiential. No ATR, slope angle, or bar count rules given. |
| Exact "counting closing prices" method for balance vs trend | Tom mentions this technique but does not demonstrate it. |
| How many bars/candles define "sustained" directional move | No specific count. Context-dependent. |
| Volatile as a formal state | Tom uses "volatile" descriptively, not as a classification. |
| Range as distinct from balance | Tom treats "range" and "sideways" as synonyms for balance. |
| Crypto-specific state adaptations (24/7, no gaps, no "opening range") | Not addressed. Crypto adaptations needed. |
| Timeframe hierarchy weights | Tom uses weekly → daily → intraday, but does not specify how to resolve conflicts. |

